  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **One In Seven** (1 review): One In Seven was introduced after banter, then split by a drum solo before returning [3]\n- **James Brown medley** (1 review): The James Brown medley closed the show as the encore [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Intro comments**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n- **Move On Up**: rare: 11 archived performances [8]\n- **Drums**: back after 26 archived shows (1049 days) [8]\n- **Vapor**: back after 34 archived shows (1134 days) [8]\n- **Vapor (cont’d)**: back after 34 archived shows (1134 days) [8]\n- **James Brown medley**: rare: 3 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2009-05-02.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 19 songs; 147 min; rated 5/5 by 5 [1]. Said about its sound: The recording sounds crisp and clear, with excellent quality; Crowd noise is low and the sound quality is strong [4][7]\n- **soulive2009-05-02.flac24**: source not stated; 10 songs; 149 min [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2009-05-02.flac16**: taped by Mike Taylor; transferred by Mike Taylor; source: Schoeps MK4v (DIN) > KCy > KS10 > VST62iU > 722 (24/96) [1]\n- **soulive2009-05-02.flac24**: taped by Mike Taylor; transferred by Mike Taylor; source: Schoeps MK4v > KCy > KS10 > VST61iU > 722 (24/96) [2]",
